From c4f4b804066a7c6ab659e2f717fd82ceaaddac86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Haudiquet <valentin.haudiquet@canonical.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:22:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/21] board: mediatek: mt8183: finish the krane configuration
 for EFI boot

Complete the krane (Lenovo IdeaPad Duet) defconfig and default
environment for the intended EFI -> GRUB -> Linux boot flow, and for
the display bring-up of the previous patches:

- CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND="bootefi bootmgr": the board has no persistent
  storage for U-Boot env variables (ENV_IS_NOWHERE), so the EFI boot
  manager boots the entries found on the ESP and falls back to the
  /EFI/BOOT/BOOTAA64.EFI removable path, both present on this target.
  distro_bootcmd would only add scan delays.  Keep a 2 s bootdelay so
  the prompt stays reachable over serial.

- Enable EFI_LOADER (explicitly disabled before) and fix the display
  driver selection: VIDEO_MT8183_DISPLAY depends on VIDEO_MIPI_DSI &&
  PANEL && PHY, which the defconfig never set, so a regenerated config
  silently dropped the cold bring-up driver and fell back to the
  (since removed) scanout choice default.  Set CONFIG_VIDEO_MIPI_DSI=y
  and select the driver explicitly so the committed defconfig is
  self-sufficient.  Drop the VIDEO_MT8183_SCANOUT line, whose driver
  no longer exists.

- Route the console through the vidconsole (stdout/stderr =
  serial,vidconsole; stdin = serial,usbkbd) in krane.env: the default
  environment must work with ENV_IS_NOWHERE at the payload stage.

- CONFIG_USE_PREBOOT=y so the "usb start" default (with USB_KEYBOARD)
  enumerates the pogo keyboard before the prompt; enable the USB stack
  (USB, DM_USB, USB_XHCI_HCD, USB_XHCI_MTK, USB_STORAGE, CMD_USB), the
  MTK T-PHY, USB_KEYBOARD and CMD_USB_MASS_STORAGE for the pogo
  keyboard and USB sticks.

- Cut CONFIG_USB_HUB_DEBOUNCE_TIMEOUT to 200 ms: with two hubs on the
  pogo bus, the stock 1000 ms adds ~2.2 s of dead wait for empty hub
  ports before the countdown can start.  Debounce only needs to cover
  the settle time of devices power-cycled by the scan itself; the
  pogo keyboard and its GL610 hub are powered from cold boot, so 200
  ms is ample.

- CONFIG_CONSOLE_ROTATION with video rot=1: the BOE TV101WUM-NL6
  panel is mounted rotated 270 degrees in the krane chassis (rotation
  property of the panel node in the upstream DT); the uclass binds the
  rotated vidconsole driver, which writes glyphs rotated by 90 degrees
  clockwise into the native 1200x1920 portrait scanout.  The
  framebuffer geometry and the depthcharge scanout path are unchanged.

- CONFIG_VIDEO_DAMAGE: with the display enabled, every console
  character went through video_sync() -> video_flush_dcache(),
  flushing the entire 1200x1920x32 (9.2 MiB) framebuffer (~144k
  cacheline maintenance ops per output character).  Dirty-rect
  tracking reduces a single typed character to one glyph region.

- CONFIG_TEXT_BASE=0x4C001000: 8-aligned image base.

- CONFIG_MT8183_SMP_PARK / park-mode residue removal, the 16x32
  console font made durable in the defconfig, and
  MTK_MEM_MAP_DDR_SIZE=0x100000000 so relocation can target the full
  4 GiB the SoC init now reports.

Signed-off-by: Valentin Haudiquet <valentin.haudiquet@canonical.com>
---
 board/mediatek/mt8183/krane.env | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 board/mediatek/mt8183/krane.env

diff --git a/board/mediatek/mt8183/krane.env b/board/mediatek/mt8183/krane.env
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..e9e8bd4ecbe
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/mediatek/mt8183/krane.env
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+stdin=serial,usbkbd
+stdout=serial,vidconsole
+stderr=serial,vidconsole
